@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "zendesk.api"

Feature: Notification Routing
	Testing the notification routing of specific tickets

Teardown:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I teardown the tickets with ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown users with the following userExternalIds from zendesk.liferay.com
	| User1  |
	| Agent1 |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds from zendesk.liferay.com
	| Organization1 |

Scenario: Notify requester of received request
	End users who create requests for specific products should receive a notification that the request was sent.

	Given I create an organization with the following values
	| Status           | Approved            |
	| Name             | Organization Name 1 |
	| Shared Tickets   | true                |
	| Shared Comments  | true                |
	| SLA              | Gold                |
	| Tier             | Regular             |
	| Support Region   | Spain               |
	| Support Language | Spanish             |
	| External ID      | Organization1       |
	And I assign an organization with organizationExternalId "Organization1" with the following tags
	| developer_tools         |
	| enterprise_search       |
	| liferay_analytics_cloud |
	| liferay_commerce        |
	| liferay_dxp             |
	| liferay_dxp_cloud       |
	| management_tools_lcs    |
	| mobile_device_detection |
	| mobile_experience       |
	| productivity_tools_sync |
	| social_office           |
	And I create a user with the following values
	| Name             | Zendesk User1                    |
	| Tags             | osb_customer,osb_kb              |
	| Password         | zendeskqauser                    |
	| Role             | End-user                         |
	| Access           | Organization                     |
	| Email            | zendesk.user1@zendesk.com.broken |
	| Phone Number     | +1 (555) 555-5555                |
	| Organization     | Organization Name 1              |
	| Language         | Spanish                          |
	| Time Zone        | Madrid                           |
	| External ID      | User1                            |
	When I create several requests as a user with the email address "zendesk.user1@zendesk.com.broken" with the following product and component values
	| prd_developer_tools         |                                       |
	| prd_enterprise_search       | monitoring                            |
	| prd_liferay_analytics_cloud |                                       |
	| prd_liferay_commerce_1_1    | activation_key_project_administration |
	| prd_liferay_commerce_2_0    | commerce_insights                     |
	| prd_liferay_commerce_2_1    | configuration_and_settings            |
	| prd_liferay_dxp_7_3         | apio_architect                        |
	| prd_liferay_dxp_7_2         | application_display_templates         |
	| prd_liferay_dxp_7_1         | audience_targeting                    |
	| prd_liferay_dxp_7_0         | authentication                        |
	| prd_liferay_dxp_cloud       | backup_recovery                       |
	| prd_management_tools_lcs    |                                       |
	| prd_mobile_device_detection |                                       |
	| prd_mobile_experience       |                                       |
	| prd_productivity_tools_sync |                                       |
	| prd_social_office           |                                       |
	And I wait for "60" seconds
	Then emails regarding the reception of the following ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" for the support language "Spanish" with the following parameters should be sent out
	| Recipients | Zendesk User1                                                                                                                           |
	| Subject    | [Soporte de Liferay] {{ticket.organization.name}} {{ticket.id}}: {{ticket.title}}                                                       |
	| Body       | Hola, {{ticket.requester.first_name}}:                                                                                                  |
	| Body       | Gracias por contactar con el Equipo de Soporte de Liferay en relación a tu proyecto {{ticket.organization.name}}                        |
	| Body       | En este momento, uno de nuestros Ingenieros de Soporte está revisando tu petición                                                       |
	| Body       | {{ticket.id}})                                                                                                                          |
	| Body       | y te contestará pronto                                                                                                                  |
	| Body       | Por favor, asegúrate que has incluido toda la información o adjuntos y si procede los pasos para reproducir el comportamiento reportado |
	| Body       | Saludos                                                                                                                                 |
	| Body       | El Equipo de Soporte de Liferay                                                                                                         |
	And "6.2" legacy ticket emails related to the following ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" for the support language "Spanish" should not be sent out
	And "6.1" legacy ticket emails related to the following ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" for the support language "Spanish" should not be sent out
	And "6.0" legacy ticket emails related to the following ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" for the support language "Spanish" should not be sent out
	And "5.2" legacy ticket emails related to the following ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" for the support language "Spanish" should not be sent out

Scenario: Notify requester of received request and 62 EOSL Policy
	End users who create requests for Liferay Portal 6.2 should receive a notification that the request was sent as well as information on the 6.2 EOSL policy.

	Given I create an organization with the following values
	| Status           | Approved            |
	| Name             | Organization Name 1 |
	| Tags             | liferay_portal      |
	| Shared Tickets   | true                |
	| Shared Comments  | true                |
	| SLA              | Gold                |
	| Tier             | Regular             |
	| Support Region   | Spain               |
	| Support Language | Spanish             |
	| External ID      | Organization1       |
	And I create a user with the following values
	| Name             | Zendesk User1                    |
	| Tags             | osb_customer,osb_kb              |
	| Password         | zendeskqauser                    |
	| Role             | End-user                         |
	| Access           | Organization                     |
	| Email            | zendesk.user1@zendesk.com.broken |
	| Phone Number     | +1 (555) 555-5555                |
	| Organization     | Organization Name 1              |
	| Language         | Spanish                          |
	| Time Zone        | Madrid                           |
	| External ID      | User1                            |
	When I create several requests as a user with the email address "zendesk.user1@zendesk.com.broken" with the following product and component values
	| prd_liferay_portal_6_2 | activation_key_project_administration |
	| prd_liferay_portal_6_2 | authentication                        |
	And I wait for "60" seconds
	Then emails regarding the reception of the following "6.2" ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" for the support language "Spanish" with the following parameters should be sent out
	| Recipients | Zendesk User1                                                                                                                           |
	| Subject    | [Soporte de Liferay] {{ticket.organization.name}} {{ticket.id}}: {{ticket.title}}                                                                                    |
	| Body       | Hola, {{ticket.requester.first_name}}:                                                                                                  |
	| Body       | Gracias por contactar al Equipo de Soporte de Liferay en relación a tu proyecto {{ticket.organization.name}}                            |
	| Body       | En este momento, uno de nuestros Ingenieros de Soporte está revisando tu petición                                                       |
	| Body       | {{ticket.id}})                                                                                                                          |
	| Body       | y te contestará pronto                                                                                                                  |
	| Body       | Ten en cuenta que el período de Soporte Premium para Liferay Portal 6.2 EE ha finalizado y el servicio de soporte es limitado           |
	| Body       | Por favor, revisa la política de fin de ciclo de vida y contacta con tu representante de ventas para conocer otras opciones disponibles |
	| Body       | Saludos                                                                                                                                 |
	| Body       | El Equipo de Soporte de Liferay                                                                                                         |
	And non-legacy ticket emails related to the following ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" for the support language "Spanish" should not be sent out

