Scenario: Notify requester of comment update
	Requesters should receive email updates when a comment has been added to their ticket.

	Given I create an organization with the following values
	| Status           | Approved            |
	| Name             | Organization Name 1 |
	| Tags             | liferay_dxp         |
	| Shared Tickets   | true                |
	| Shared Comments  | true                |
	| SLA              | Gold                |
	| Tier             | Regular             |
	| Support Region   | Spain               |
	| Support Language | Spanish             |
	| External ID      | Organization1       |
	And I create a user with the following values
	| Name             | Zendesk User1                    |
	| Tags             | osb_customer,osb_kb              |
	| Password         | zendeskqauser                    |
	| Role             | End-user                         |
	| Access           | Organization                     |
	| Email            | zendesk.user1@zendesk.com.broken |
	| Phone Number     | +1 (555) 555-5555                |
	| Organization     | Organization Name 1              |
	| Language         | Spanish                          |
	| Time Zone        | Madrid                           |
	| External ID      | User1                            |
	And I create a user with the following values
	| Name             | Zendesk Agent1                    |
	| Password         | zendeskqauser                     |
	| Role             | Agent                             |
	| Email            | zendesk.agent1@liferay.com.broken |
	| Phone Number     | +1 (555) 555-5555                 |
	| Language         | Spanish                           |
	| Time Zone        | Pacific Time (US & Canada)        |
	| External ID      | Agent1                            |
	And I assign the user with the email address "zendesk.agent1@liferay.com.broken" to the group "CSE - US"
	When I create a request as a user with the email address "zendesk.user1@zendesk.com.broken" with the following values
	| Product                  | prd_liferay_dxp_7_3                              |
	| Component                | apio_architect                                   |
	| System Status            | production_functioning_with_limited_capabilities |
	| Subject                  | Request Subject                                  |
	| Description              | Request Description                              |
	| Organization External ID | Organization1                                    |
	And I assign the ticket with the ID "${staticRequestIdList}" to a user with the email address "zendesk.agent1@liferay.com.broken"
	And I create a comment with the content "Comment Body" on a request with the ID "${staticRequestIdList}" as a user with the email address "zendesk.agent1@liferay.com.broken"
	Then an email regarding the comment with the body "Comment Body" added to a ticket with the ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" for the support language "Spanish" containing the following parameters should be sent out to the ticket requester
	| Recipients | Zendesk User1                                                                         |
	| Subject    | Re: [Soporte de Liferay] {{ticket.organization.name}} {{ticket.id}}: {{ticket.title}} |
	| Body       | Hola, {{ticket.requester.first_name}}                                                 |
	| Body       | Tu ticket                                                                             |
	| Body       | {{ticket.id}}) ha sido actualizado                                                    |
	| Body       | {{ticket.latest_public_comment_formatted}}                                            |

Scenario: Notify assignee of comment update
	Assignees should receive email updates when a comment has been added to their ticket.

	Given I create an organization with the following values
	| Status           | Approved            |
	| Name             | Organization Name 1 |
	| Tags             | liferay_dxp         |
	| Shared Tickets   | true                |
	| Shared Comments  | true                |
	| SLA              | Gold                |
	| Tier             | Regular             |
	| Support Region   | Spain               |
	| Support Language | Spanish             |
	| External ID      | Organization1       |
	And I create a user with the following values
	| Name             | Zendesk User1                    |
	| Tags             | osb_customer,osb_kb              |
	| Password         | zendeskqauser                    |
	| Role             | End-user                         |
	| Access           | Organization                     |
	| Email            | zendesk.user1@zendesk.com.broken |
	| Phone Number     | +1 (555) 555-5555                |
	| Organization     | Organization Name 1              |
	| Language         | Spanish                          |
	| Time Zone        | Madrid                           |
	| External ID      | User1                            |
	And I create a user with the following values
	| Name             | Zendesk Agent1                    |
	| Password         | zendeskqauser                     |
	| Role             | Agent                             |
	| Email            | zendesk.agent1@liferay.com.broken |
	| Phone Number     | +1 (555) 555-5555                 |
	| Language         | Spanish                           |
	| Time Zone        | Pacific Time (US & Canada)        |
	| External ID      | Agent1                            |
	And I assign the user with the email address "zendesk.agent1@liferay.com.broken" to the group "CSE - US"
	When I create a request as a user with the email address "zendesk.user1@zendesk.com.broken" with the following values
	| Product                  | prd_liferay_dxp_7_3                              |
	| Component                | apio_architect                                   |
	| System Status            | production_functioning_with_limited_capabilities |
	| Subject                  | Request Subject                                  |
	| Description              | Request Description                              |
	| Organization External ID | Organization1                                    |
	And I assign the ticket with the ID "${staticRequestIdList}" to a user with the email address "zendesk.agent1@liferay.com.broken"
	And I create a comment with the content "Comment Body" on a request with the ID "${staticRequestIdList}" as a user with the email address "zendesk.user1@zendesk.com.broken"
	Then an email regarding the comment with the body "Comment Body" added to a ticket with the ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" for the support language "Spanish" containing the following parameters should be sent out to the ticket assignee
	| Recipients | Zendesk Agent1                                      |
	| Subject    | [{{ticket.organization.name}}] Re: {{ticket.title}} |
	| Body       | El ticket                                           |
	| Body       | {{ticket.id}}) ha sido actualizado                  |
	| Body       | {{ticket.latest_comment_formatted}}                 |

Scenario: Notify assignee of assignment
	Assignees should receive email updates when a ticket is assigned to them.

	Given I create an organization with the following values
	| Status           | Approved            |
	| Name             | Organization Name 1 |
	| Tags             | liferay_dxp         |
	| Shared Tickets   | true                |
	| Shared Comments  | true                |
	| SLA              | Gold                |
	| Tier             | Regular             |
	| Support Region   | Spain               |
	| Support Language | Spanish             |
	| External ID      | Organization1       |
	And I create a user with the following values
	| Name             | Zendesk User1                    |
	| Tags             | osb_customer,osb_kb              |
	| Password         | zendeskqauser                    |
	| Role             | End-user                         |
	| Access           | Organization                     |
	| Email            | zendesk.user1@zendesk.com.broken |
	| Phone Number     | +1 (555) 555-5555                |
	| Organization     | Organization Name 1              |
	| Language         | Spanish                          |
	| Time Zone        | Madrid                           |
	| External ID      | User1                            |
	And I create a user with the following values
	| Name             | Zendesk Agent1                    |
	| Password         | zendeskqauser                     |
	| Role             | Agent                             |
	| Email            | zendesk.agent1@liferay.com.broken |
	| Phone Number     | +1 (555) 555-5555                 |
	| Language         | Spanish                           |
	| Time Zone        | Pacific Time (US & Canada)        |
	| External ID      | Agent1                            |
	And I assign the user with the email address "zendesk.agent1@liferay.com.broken" to the group "CSE - US"
	When I create a request as a user with the email address "zendesk.user1@zendesk.com.broken" with the following values
	| Product                  | prd_liferay_dxp_7_3                              |
	| Component                | apio_architect                                   |
	| System Status            | production_functioning_with_limited_capabilities |
	| Subject                  | Request Subject                                  |
	| Description              | Request Description                              |
	| Organization External ID | Organization1                                    |
	And I assign the ticket with the ID "${staticRequestIdList}" to a user with the email address "zendesk.agent1@liferay.com.broken"
	Then an email regarding an assignment to ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" for the support language "Spanish" containing the following parameters should be sent out to the ticket assignee
	| Recipients | Zendesk Agent1                                              |
